WEBVTT

00:02.690 --> 00:06.736
[Lindelof] Hello there. This is
Damon Lindelof. And I'm here with...

00:06.819 --> 00:10.281
- [Mitchell] Elizabeth Mitchell.
- [Lindelof] Elizabeth is in Hawaii.

00:10.364 --> 00:13.367
I'm in Los Angeles
and we're talking in our NPR voices,

00:13.451 --> 00:15.369
SO you can watch this commentary.

00:15.453 --> 00:19.373
And we're gonna be talking today
about episode one,

00:19.457 --> 00:24.128
the season premiere of, uh, of
season three, A Tale Of Two Cities,

00:24.212 --> 00:28.925
which just so happens to be the episode
in which we introduce Juliet.

00:30.051 --> 00:31.135
[Mitchell] Juliet?

00:31.219 --> 00:34.347
- [Lindelof] That's your character.
- [Mitchell] Oh, there's me.

00:34.430 --> 00:38.226
- [Lindelof] That's you. Your eye.
- [Mitchell] Oh. [laughs] Wasn't it fun?

00:38.309 --> 00:42.730
[Lindelof] I will say, you are one of
the best eye-actresses in Hollywood.

00:42.813 --> 00:44.899
[Mitchell] Aw, Damon, stop. Really?

00:44.982 --> 00:48.069
[Lindelof] You nailed that eye-open
in one take. Yeah, it's good.

00:48.152 --> 00:49.278
[Mitchell] Well, yeah.

00:49.362 --> 00:52.114
[Lindelof] You're doing some
eye acting here as well.

00:52.198 --> 00:55.660
[Mitchell] Well, I do a lot
of eye acting. I start with the eye.

00:55.743 --> 00:57.912
- [Lindelof] It shows.
- [Mitchell laughing]

00:57.995 --> 00:59.330
[Lindelof] Just a little...

00:59.413 --> 01:01.666
[Mitchell] You know,
this song has now taken off.

01:01.749 --> 01:04.752
[Lindelof] It... Oh, yeah, has it?
Really? This is Petula Clark.

01:04.835 --> 01:07.922
[Mitchell] Once again,
you've started something. Yeah.

01:08.005 --> 01:10.925
[Lindelof] All the music we use
on the show is basically

01:11.008 --> 01:13.594
music that my mother
used to vacuum to on Sundays.

01:13.678 --> 01:17.848
And she'd cry while she vacuumed. She'd
listen to Mama Cass and Petula Clark.

01:17.932 --> 01:21.310
And I said, "I am gonna use
all those songs on the show."

01:22.353 --> 01:24.855
- [Mitchell] I'm glad you did.
- [Lindelof] Good song.

01:24.939 --> 01:28.109
[Mitchell] It's presented
kind of a timeless... It has.

01:28.192 --> 01:31.904
[Lindelof] Now, there was actually
another scene that we shot before...

01:31.988 --> 01:33.447
...uh, right after this one.

01:33.531 --> 01:36.993
And, obviously, we're doing the big
psych-out here that we are...

01:37.076 --> 01:39.578
...we are, in fact, back in,
back in the real world.

01:39.662 --> 01:42.957
And we've never met this woman,
and we don't know whose legs those are,

01:43.040 --> 01:45.042
- etcetera, etcetera.
- [Mitchell] Yeah.

01:47.712 --> 01:49.964
[Lindelof] Do you want to tell us
about the scene

01:50.047 --> 01:53.801
that we so egregiously cut
before this book club scene?

01:53.884 --> 01:57.346
[Mitchell laughs] Well, there were
a couple little snippets, actually.

01:57.430 --> 02:00.266
There was the one where
I'm looking at the x-rays, um...

02:00.349 --> 02:03.602
And we kind of wonder who they are.
And, uh...

02:03.686 --> 02:07.940
And there was also a really great scene
between me and the other actress, Julia.

02:08.024 --> 02:11.610
[Lindelof] She was actually the woman in
The Creature From The Black Lagoon.

02:11.694 --> 02:14.238
- When you see that...
- [Mitchell] Which is amazing...

02:14.322 --> 02:16.073
[Lindelof] ...she's the main chick.

02:16.157 --> 02:19.827
She's the one the creature is carrying
out of the lagoon, so... there she is.

02:19.910 --> 02:22.747
[Mitchell] She was such
a pleasure. She was so much fun.

02:22.830 --> 02:26.459
Um, and we had, and we did have
a good one where she was talking to me

02:26.542 --> 02:30.629
about the fact that she thinks
Ben might have feelings for me,

02:30.713 --> 02:34.592
and have I talked to him about it.
And... I think I growl at her. [laughs]

02:34.675 --> 02:38.012
[Lindelof] The irony is that we set up
the whole tumor thing right there,

02:38.095 --> 02:40.848
then we cut it out of the show.
So people could later accuse us

02:40.931 --> 02:43.392
- of making it up as we went along.
- [Mitchell] You did.

02:43.476 --> 02:46.228
[Lindelof] I think it'll be
in the deleted scenes, though.

02:47.063 --> 02:50.358
[Mitchell] I always thought it was
something more, which it kind of was.

02:50.441 --> 02:52.360
So you guys are very clever that way.

02:52.443 --> 02:55.321
- And there he is.
- [Lindelof] There's Mr. Benjamin Linus.

02:55.404 --> 02:58.366
[Mitchell] This is good.
This was fun to watch him do this.

02:58.449 --> 03:01.202
[Lindelof] When did you
shoot this stuff? Was this kind of,

03:01.285 --> 03:04.872
- you did the stuff in the Hydra first?
- [Mitchell] This was my first day.

03:04.955 --> 03:07.666
Well, actually, I think we might
have done a little Hydra,

03:07.750 --> 03:10.169
but then, this was either
my first or my second day.

03:10.252 --> 03:12.671
[Lindelof] What was it like
meeting Michael Emerson

03:12.755 --> 03:14.924
when you first came to Hawaii
and you were like,

03:15.007 --> 03:17.385
"Hi, we're gonna be doing
some scenes together"?

03:17.468 --> 03:19.804
- Tell me that story.
- [Mitchell laughing]

03:19.887 --> 03:22.348
I think I might have been...
I can't remember it.

03:22.431 --> 03:26.268
I know in this particular scene I was
giving him a hard time about something,

03:26.352 --> 03:30.231
he turned to me, straight-faced, those
blue eyes looking right at me, he goes,

03:30.314 --> 03:32.566
"I can't work with you, you know?"
[laughs]

03:32.650 --> 03:34.318
And I was like, "fine,"

03:34.402 --> 03:37.738
- but I can't remember what it was.
- [Lindelof] Then he tried to Kill you.

03:37.822 --> 03:39.532
[Mitchell] Seemed like someone ll...

03:39.615 --> 03:43.786
Then he tried to kill me, yeah...
which I thought, "Hey, let him try."

03:43.869 --> 03:46.288
- [Lindelof] Exactly.
- [Mitchell] That's worth it.

03:46.372 --> 03:49.917
[Lindelof] You got to wake up
pretty early in the morning to kill him.

03:50.501 --> 03:53.587
[Mitchell] You know, poor, poor Ethan.
He, you know, he...

03:53.671 --> 03:55.756
He hates being thought of as creepy,

03:55.840 --> 03:59.927
'cause he's so very straight with what
he does. But he is, he is pretty creepy.

04:00.010 --> 04:02.012
[Lindelof] Ethan wins the kind of, like,

04:02.096 --> 04:06.517
I Died Forever Ago, But I Keep
Cropping Up In The Show Award,

04:06.600 --> 04:10.104
- 'cause he's just that good.
- [Mitchell] You have to have him.

04:10.187 --> 04:13.274
- He's an excellent creepy antagonist.
- [Lindelof] He's awesome.

04:13.357 --> 04:16.652
And there it goes, and we know what
Goodwin is now, which is kind of fun.

04:16.735 --> 04:20.573
[Lindelof] Yeah. That's right. I wonder
how Juliet reacted when Goodwin died.

04:20.656 --> 04:25.035
- I'd like to see that story.
- [Mitchell laughs] Well, I would too.

04:25.119 --> 04:28.456
"Cause it's Juliet. That scene,
by the way, that completely...

04:28.539 --> 04:31.292
My husband's mouth was hanging open,
which was so much fun.

04:31.375 --> 04:33.335
[Lindelof] Jack Bender
directed this...

04:33.419 --> 04:36.338
- [Mitchell] Nice to shock him.
- [Lindelof] ...phenomenally.

04:36.422 --> 04:38.507
[Mitchell] He really kept it going.

04:40.217 --> 04:41.510
[Lindelof] So here we are,
we're gonna, we're going to, uh,

04:41.510 --> 04:43.137
[Lindelof] So here we are,
we're gonna, we're going to, uh,

04:43.220 --> 04:48.142
to have some Jack flashbacks here,
which, uh, which is... is wonderful and,

04:48.225 --> 04:50.978
and, uh, and thought-provoking
and emotional.

04:51.061 --> 04:54.440
But since Elizabeth isn't
in them, really, who cares?

04:54.523 --> 04:57.318
- [Mitchell laughing]
- [Lindelof] So what ...

04:57.401 --> 05:00.905
- what I feel that people might be...
- [Mitchell] I care, I gotta tell you.

05:00.988 --> 05:03.824
- He's fun to watch, but go ahead.
- [Lindelof] Oh, Jack's sad.

05:03.908 --> 05:08.078
He's gonna yell, like, oh, he still
likes his ex-wife. There she is.

05:08.162 --> 05:10.789
- This is an awesome...
- [Mitchell] She looks so pretty.

05:10.873 --> 05:14.460
- [Lindelof] She's amazing. And, uh...
- [Mitchell] This is an awesome scene.

05:14.543 --> 05:18.130
[Lindelof] What's really cool is that
Julie Bowen, you know, you kind of...

05:18.214 --> 05:19.840
I wouldn't say you look like her,

05:19.924 --> 05:23.302
but you definitely are in that
wheelhouse of that type, you know?

05:23.385 --> 05:26.180
So we understand instantly
why Jack is drawn to Juliet.

05:26.263 --> 05:30.142
- [Mitchell] Absolutely. A softness...
- [Lindelof] There's good eye-acting.

05:30.226 --> 05:34.188
[Mitchell] That was... Well,
I learned from him, maybe.

05:34.271 --> 05:37.358
And there's some chains,
Jack in chains.

05:37.441 --> 05:39.026
[dramatically] Jack in chains.

05:39.109 --> 05:41.529
- There's some muscles.
- [Lindelof] A lot of chains.

05:41.612 --> 05:44.448
[Mitchell] A lot of chains and
a lot of muscles and some sweat.

05:44.532 --> 05:45.866
These aren't all bad things.

05:45.950 --> 05:49.703
[Lindelof] It wouldn't be Lost if there
weren't chains and sweat, and Band-Aids.

05:49.787 --> 05:52.623
- [Mitchell laughs] And muscles.
- [Lindelof] Cotton balls.

05:52.706 --> 05:55.334
There's Elizabeth Mitchell's name
for the first time,

05:55.417 --> 05:57.211
exciting to see you amongst the cast.

05:57.294 --> 05:59.505
[Mitchell] Oh, that was really fun.

05:59.588 --> 06:01.840
[Lindelof] Can you
talk us through a bit about,

06:01.924 --> 06:03.634
through the auditioning process?

06:03.717 --> 06:06.845
What was it like when
you first got a call saying,

06:06.929 --> 06:10.015
"Hey, they're gonna be adding
this new character to Lost"?

06:11.183 --> 06:15.062
[Mitchell] Well, you guys called a while
just to say they were adding a character

06:15.145 --> 06:19.191
or somebody did. Maybe it was Jeff.
But I know that, uh, we got the call,

06:19.275 --> 06:22.236
and I thought to myself...
- [Lindelof] There was no glass there.

06:22.319 --> 06:26.740
Matthew completely just acted that.
He mimed it, that's how good he is.

06:26.824 --> 06:31.078
There's still... there's still no glass.
Have you ever seen a mime in a box?

06:31.161 --> 06:34.415
- That's what he's doing, no glass.
- [Mitchell] He's a beautiful mime.

06:34.498 --> 06:37.668
You've seen his whiteface, right?
He can really do it. He fantastic.

06:37.751 --> 06:41.046
[Lindelof] When he does
the tug o' war thing, unbelievable.

06:41.130 --> 06:42.423
Classic miming.

06:42.506 --> 06:47.094
[Mitchell] Well, yeah. No, he can
do it all. And then, box over his head.

06:47.177 --> 06:49.221
[Lindelof] Oh, that's a classic.

06:49.305 --> 06:51.265
[muffled] Can you hear me?!

06:51.348 --> 06:55.227
[Lindelof] The reason that Elizabeth and
I are completely talking over each other

06:55.311 --> 06:57.855
is there is a one-second delay
between us and Hawaii.

06:57.938 --> 07:02.109
So it isn't that we aren't cracking each
other up, it's just it takes a second

07:02.192 --> 07:06.280
for me to say something funny and
for her to register it, and vice-versa.

07:06.363 --> 07:11.285
- So, you know?
- [Mitchell laughing] Yeah.

07:11.368 --> 07:13.621
Oh, Kate.

07:13.704 --> 07:14.788
Where am 1?2?

07:14.872 --> 07:17.583
You don't really think
I'm going to answer that, do you?

07:17.666 --> 07:21.295
- [Lindelof] And there's M.C. Gainey.
- [Mitchell] He looks so big and scary,

07:21.378 --> 07:23.922
- and the nicest guy in the world.
- [Lindelof] The best.

07:24.006 --> 07:26.634
Sorry, I interrupted your story.
You were saying...?

07:26.717 --> 07:29.261
[Mitchell] No, no.
Then, then, of course, um,

07:29.345 --> 07:33.140
I didn't think it would ever happen.
And then, like, the people kept calling,

07:33.223 --> 07:35.559
"We think you might."
I said, "I don't believe it."

07:35.643 --> 07:38.437
I'll believe it when I see it."
And then, of course, I went in.

07:38.520 --> 07:41.482
And someone came out and
then gave me a note about Juliet,

07:41.565 --> 07:44.151
which was pretty much
exactly the way I wanted to do it,

07:44.234 --> 07:45.944
which made me very happy.

07:46.028 --> 07:49.490
And I saw pretty much
every actress that I've known

07:49.573 --> 07:53.661
or been around for the past ten years.
And it was, it was kind of fun.

07:53.744 --> 07:56.538
It was kind of a fun experience.
You guys were hilarious.

07:56.622 --> 07:58.916
Jeff was there.
I don't think you were in the room.

07:58.999 --> 08:00.834
[Lindelof] I think Pinkner was there

08:00.918 --> 08:04.338
- for the first time you did the read.
- [Mitchell] Yeah, yeah he was.

08:04.421 --> 08:07.966
[Lindelof] I try never to let
anybody see me, um, you know.

08:08.050 --> 08:11.845
- [Mitchell laughing]
- [Lindelof] I'm kinda very mysterious.

08:11.929 --> 08:14.348
[Mitchell] The man behind the curtain
kind of thing?

08:14.431 --> 08:15.849
[Lindelof] Exactly what it is.

08:15.933 --> 08:19.019
I've got a very kind of
Jacob-like quality to me...

08:19.103 --> 08:22.231
...inthat I live in a dirty cabin
and like to break things.

08:22.314 --> 08:26.026
[Mitchell] Well, of course,
yeah, you're spectral.

08:27.319 --> 08:30.239
[Lindelof] What's interesting about
watching this stuff now,

08:30.322 --> 08:34.201
I haven't seen this episode in a long
time, we spend lots of hours editing.

08:34.284 --> 08:37.246
But, you know, this is
our first time in the cages.

08:37.329 --> 08:41.583
And the fact that we are gonna spend
the next five hours of the show, plus,

08:41.667 --> 08:44.461
sort of confined in these things
makes me begin to realize

08:44.545 --> 08:48.215
why the audience got so angry at us
for such a period of time

08:48.298 --> 08:51.552
in terms of keeping the beautiful
Josh Holloway caged in,

08:51.635 --> 08:53.637
<i>in 2 polar-bear cage pushing buttons,</i>

08:53.721 --> 08:57.641
when he could be out running around,
taking his shirt off more often.

08:59.351 --> 09:02.312
[Mitchell] Well, he does take his
shirt off in the cage, though.

09:02.396 --> 09:05.190
And, and I think that was, uh,
that was nice, you know?

09:05.274 --> 09:09.069
- It's something to give to people.
- [Lindelof] We got around to that.

09:09.903 --> 09:11.739
[Mitchell] Of course you did.

09:11.822 --> 09:14.491
And the two of them in cages
opposite of each other.

09:14.575 --> 09:18.078
[Lindelof] This is a lot like the cage
that we keep you in, right, Elizabeth?

09:18.162 --> 09:20.289
- Down in Hawaii?
- [Mitchell] Well, you know,

09:20.372 --> 09:23.751
it's really best for me to perform at,
at peak efficiency

09:23.834 --> 09:28.255
if I am kept in a polar-bear cage.
I requested that cage.

09:28.338 --> 09:30.924
- [Lindelof] This one here.
- [Mitchell] But whatever.

09:31.008 --> 09:34.595
[Lindelof] There's Karl. That's some
good back acting, by the way.

09:34.678 --> 09:36.889
[Mitchell] Some really good back acting.

09:36.972 --> 09:40.100
[Lindelof] We told the actor the
camera was on the other side of him,

09:40.184 --> 09:42.811
and he had no idea
that we were shooting that.

09:42.895 --> 09:48.734
- No, I, I joke.
- [Mitchell laughing] I, I joke.

09:48.817 --> 09:50.778
[Lindelof] It's amazing. There's Karl.

09:50.861 --> 09:54.281
Who would know at that time that Karl
would become such an integral force?

09:54.364 --> 09:56.325
He would be the Paul Revere
of the island.

09:56.408 --> 09:58.619
[Mitchell] I know.

09:58.702 --> 10:02.289
- He's, and he's, he is a great kid.
- [Lindelof] Blake is his name, yes?

10:02.372 --> 10:05.793
[Mitchell] This is my problem.
I have nothing catty to say of Blake.

10:05.876 --> 10:09.630
[Lindelof] Here he is again. No glass.
Leaning up against nothing.

10:09.713 --> 10:11.799
[Mitchell] Chains, of course.

10:12.716 --> 10:15.427
He even made his palms
do that kind of indentation thing.

10:15.511 --> 10:17.554
[Lindelof] This is actually
a great moment,

10:17.638 --> 10:20.390
because in the tone meeting
which we have with Jack Bender,

10:20.474 --> 10:22.768
basically, he was reading the script
and going,

10:22.851 --> 10:25.771
"What is Jack exactly
trying to do here?"

10:25.854 --> 10:28.732
I said, "He's trying to pull
on the chain." And he said, "Why?"

10:28.816 --> 10:32.110
And I said, "Don't worry,
Foxy'll sell it." And, lo and behold...

10:32.194 --> 10:35.280
I don't know what... I don't know
what his plan is, but he sold it.

10:35.364 --> 10:37.241
- So here you are.
- [Mitchell] I know.

10:37.324 --> 10:40.661
[Lindelof] Now, everyone's...
"I'm Juliet." There it is.

10:42.079 --> 10:43.247
[Mitchell] Yeah. What a great, great way
to have someone come into a show.

10:43.247 --> 10:45.999
[Mitchell] Yeah. What a great, great way
to have someone come into a show.

10:46.083 --> 10:48.502
Just that.
That was awesome.

10:48.585 --> 10:52.172
[Lindelof] It's cool, because it's after
we've seen her. We've seen her cry,

10:52.256 --> 10:54.466
We're sort of emotionally
bonded to her, and...

10:54.550 --> 10:58.011
- We don't know anything about her.
- [Mitchell] Don't expect it to be her.

10:58.095 --> 11:00.931
- [Lindelof] Exactly.
- [Mitchell] Yeah. And there she is.

11:01.014 --> 11:04.810
Ohh. Oh, obsessive Jack.

11:04.893 --> 11:08.438
[Lindelof] He is, uh, you don't want
Jack to get a crush on you,

11:09.439 --> 11:13.360
- 'cause it's just a matter of time.
- [Mitchell] Well... yeah.

11:13.443 --> 11:17.364
And it, it could be used against him,
but it is, it's a weakness, but sweet.

11:17.447 --> 11:19.992
[Lindelof] I think Juliet's
kind of got a crush on Jack.

11:20.075 --> 11:24.955
I would have to say, um, you know,
that, uh, from the very beginning,

11:25.038 --> 11:27.583
she totally feels the heat
even through that,

11:27.666 --> 11:31.128
even through that, uh,
that glass, uh, wall there.

11:31.211 --> 11:34.006
[Mitchell] Well, maybe,
maybe the glass just started it.

11:34.089 --> 11:35.841
It was his impressive glass acting.

11:35.924 --> 11:38.343
It's kind of like a microwave in there,
heating up...

11:38.427 --> 11:42.639
- [Mitchell laughing]
- [Lindelof] ...behind the glass.

11:42.723 --> 11:46.727
Juliet might, might as well walk over
and just push the popcorn button,

11:46.810 --> 11:52.232
- 'cause it's getting hot up in there.
- [Mitchell laughing]

11:52.316 --> 11:55.652
- So take off all your clothes.
- [Lindelof chuckles]

11:55.736 --> 11:58.530
- Right now?
- [Mitchell laughs]

11:58.614 --> 12:01.825
I was just, "It's getting hot in
here, so take off all your clothes..."

12:01.909 --> 12:05.203
[Lindelof] You know what? You're
in Hawaii, and I'm in L.A., why not?

12:05.287 --> 12:08.665
Otherwise, it would be unprofessional.
But just let me remove...

12:08.749 --> 12:12.085
[Mitchell] You're absolutely right.
You don't want to make me feel bad.

12:12.169 --> 12:15.714
- [Lindelof] I wouldn't.
- [Mitchell laughing]

12:15.797 --> 12:17.758
[Lindelof] Julie Bowen is so awesome.

12:17.841 --> 12:20.344
I love using her
over and over again on this show.

12:20.427 --> 12:23.805
[Mitchell] She not only is awesome
on camera, she's awesome in person.

12:23.889 --> 12:26.850
We met a couple years ago.
And it's, she's just great.

12:26.934 --> 12:28.936
You have nothing to say
but "she's great."

12:29.019 --> 12:30.520
[Lindelof] The scene we shot...

12:30.604 --> 12:32.606
[Mitchell] A man's woman,
a woman's woman.

12:32.689 --> 12:36.610
[Lindelof] ...in Jack's flashbacks in
the finale, she's eight months pregnant.

12:36.693 --> 12:39.696
- We actually shot it in L_A.
- [Mitchell] I bet she looks Insane.

12:39.780 --> 12:42.282
[Lindelof] Awesome.
We went to set, and she was, like,

12:42.366 --> 12:44.993
"Hi, how are you?"
Like, you know, happy to work.

12:45.994 --> 12:48.789
[Lindelof] And we're, like,
"Thanks for doing this so soon,

12:48.872 --> 12:51.249
close to your imminent due date."
And she was, like,

12:51.333 --> 12:54.878
- "Ah, whatever." Very cool.
- [Mitchell] "Whatever," of course.

12:54.962 --> 12:58.298
[Lindelof] I love... She's got
the greatest attitude. The best.

12:58.382 --> 13:00.425
[Mitchell] She has
the greatest attitude.

13:00.509 --> 13:02.052
She's so much fun to be around.

13:04.137 --> 13:08.183
[Lindelof] So here's your first big
scene. And this was your audition scene.

13:09.226 --> 13:11.645
[Mitchell] This was my audition scene.

13:11.728 --> 13:14.982
And it was very similar
to the way I kind of saw it.

13:15.983 --> 13:17.734
But it was...

13:19.069 --> 13:20.404
[Mitchell chuckles]

13:22.155 --> 13:25.242
You know, I didn't realize at the time
that I was talking down to him,

13:25.325 --> 13:27.995
- but it is interesting.
- [Lindelof] You are very much...

13:28.078 --> 13:30.956
- [Mitchell] I think she likes him.
- [Lindelof] She likes him.

13:31.039 --> 13:34.251
But you're very much sort of the,
you know, sixth-grade teacher here,

13:34.334 --> 13:36.628
and he's very much the kid who is,

13:36.712 --> 13:40.465
you know, sort of, you know,
talking to his friends in class.

13:40.549 --> 13:41.633
Ah.

13:41.717 --> 13:44.511
[Mitchell] But you get the idea
that she wants to help him.

13:44.594 --> 13:48.557
[Lindelof] Look at this gratuitous...
Kate showering.

13:48.640 --> 13:51.643
Do we really need that in the show?
Does that make it a better show?

13:51.727 --> 13:55.522
[Mitchell] Yeah. I think it does,
actually. I think it does.

13:56.398 --> 13:58.734
It gives her the vulnerability.

13:58.817 --> 14:02.529
"Wear this." Oh, my gosh, you guys.
It's always, it's great.

14:02.612 --> 14:06.616
You have all these people you can play
with, like figurines when you're a kid.

14:06.700 --> 14:09.119
You can make them do
whatever you want. It's awesome.

14:09.202 --> 14:11.705
[Lindelof] Well, not whatever we want.

14:11.788 --> 14:14.958
[Mitchell laughing]

14:16.543 --> 14:19.463
- You can take the show to cable.
- [Lindelof] Yeah. That's true.

14:19.546 --> 14:22.340
[Mitchell] Oh. Kate in a dress.

14:25.469 --> 14:27.888
[Lindelof] Yeah.
This was a cool idea, you know.

14:27.971 --> 14:32.392
I think... J.J. and I actually wrote the
script together and, uh, you know,

14:32.476 --> 14:35.437
this, this idea was based on
Raiders Of The Lost Ark.

14:35.520 --> 14:40.484
And basically, there's a scene where,
uh, where, um, Marion Ravenwood,

14:40.567 --> 14:45.906
played by, uh, Karen Allen, is
basically, she's caught by the bad guys.

14:45.989 --> 14:49.159
And she's been, like,
tied up in this tent the entire time.

14:49.242 --> 14:52.412
And he brings in this beautiful dress.
And she's such a tomboy,

14:52.496 --> 14:54.748
and has been rocking
and rolling the entire time,

14:54.831 --> 14:58.502
it completely, like, makes her
so vulnerable when she puts it on.

14:58.585 --> 15:00.087
[Mitchell] It really does.

15:00.170 --> 15:03.590
[Lindelof] We were like, "How would Ben
make Kate really vulnerable here?

15:03.673 --> 15:06.009
Oh, let's put her in a nice dress."

15:09.513 --> 15:12.057
[Mitchell] And give her some silverware.

15:12.140 --> 15:14.726
[Lindelof] Oh, exactly.
Silverware is a great way

15:14.810 --> 15:18.855
to make somebody feel vulnerable. That's
why I eat all my food with toothpicks.

15:18.939 --> 15:20.774
[Mitchell laughing]

15:20.857 --> 15:23.777
[Lindelof] Does that make me crazy?
Am I eccentric for that?

15:23.860 --> 15:27.572
[Mitchell laughs] Well, not for that.

15:27.656 --> 15:31.535
[Lindelof] This, uh, this French press,
I think, was Carlton Cuse's idea.

15:31.618 --> 15:34.996
- He was, like, when I first said...
- [Mitchell] That is such a good idea.

15:35.080 --> 15:38.291
And Ben should have this whole,
like, breakfast set up, like at the,

15:38.375 --> 15:39.876
you know, like at a resort.

15:39.960 --> 15:42.963
And he should go...
And there should be a French press.

15:43.046 --> 15:45.423
- And, and there it is.
- [Mitchell] That's so good.

15:45.507 --> 15:49.052
[Lindelof] It's just sitting there,
like a time bomb waiting to go off,

15:49.136 --> 15:53.223
like the old Road Runner cartoons,
as he pushes it down. I love it.

15:53.306 --> 15:57.352
[Mitchell] Something a little Planet Of
The Apes too, the first one, of course.

15:57.435 --> 16:01.064
[Lindelof] With the French press? Here's
Kate's love affair with handcuffs.

16:01.148 --> 16:04.526
[Mitchell] Well, not the French press.
Just the, this whole... [laughs]

16:04.609 --> 16:07.112
[Lindelof] Isn't that what's
on the Statue Of Liberty

16:07.195 --> 16:09.573
at the end of Planet Of The Apes?
She's got the torch,

16:09.656 --> 16:12.826
and she's holding a big French press,
and Charlton Heston's like,

16:12.909 --> 16:16.621
"You destroyed it all
with your French presses!

16:16.705 --> 16:19.583
- It was the coffee!"
- [Mitchell laughing]

16:19.666 --> 16:22.669
[Lindelof] That is in
the original cut, actually.

16:22.752 --> 16:25.338
Or I might, I might be
thinking of Soylent Green.

16:25.422 --> 16:28.383
- [Mitchell] I did not know that.
- [Lindelof] I'm not sure.

16:30.802 --> 16:32.470
I love that he has the ketchup...

16:32.554 --> 16:35.015
[Mitchell] He's actually quite
threatening in this.

16:35.098 --> 16:39.477
- [Lindelof] Yeah, he's pissed.
- [Mitchell] He does. Yeah.

16:39.561 --> 16:41.354
No, he's, he's a little scary.

16:41.438 --> 16:45.108
- I never think of him as scary. But...
- [Lindelof] He's been taking beatings.

16:45.192 --> 16:47.944
Remember Ben for the better part
of the end of the last season

16:48.028 --> 16:51.448
was just getting beat-up all the time.
He still has these scars on his face.

16:51.531 --> 16:54.201
- It's great.
- [Mitchell] He was a punching bag.

16:54.284 --> 16:55.577
He did it so nicely.

16:55.660 --> 16:57.537
[Lindelof] Not easy
to be a punching bag.

16:57.621 --> 16:59.372
[Mitchell] Those eyes are amazing.

17:00.373 --> 17:04.336
[Lindelof] I look at this scene, I feel
like we shot in front of a green screen,

17:04.419 --> 17:09.174
'cause, uh, that... that view behind him
is 80 amazing. But that is the location.

17:09.966 --> 17:12.886
[Mitchell] That's what happens
when you drive around Hawaii.

17:12.969 --> 17:15.180
You can't believe
the color of the water.

17:16.806 --> 17:18.767
It looks like something they made up.

17:18.850 --> 17:21.561
But, you're right,
it looks like a green screen.

17:21.645 --> 17:25.774
[Lindelof] Here he is explaining what
the next six episodes are gonna be.

17:26.983 --> 17:30.779
[Mitchell] How can they do this to her?
She looks like she's seven years old.

17:31.655 --> 17:33.198
[Mitchell laughs]

17:33.281 --> 17:36.034
[Lindelof] See, audience who hated
the first six episodes?

17:36.117 --> 17:39.913
Ben told you that you wouldn't like
them. He told you they'd be unpleasant.

17:39.996 --> 17:43.500
[Mitchell laughing] They told you
you wouldn't like them. Oh, no.

17:43.500 --> 17:44.000
[Mitchell laughing] They told you
you wouldn't like them. Oh, no.

17:44.084 --> 17:47.754
[Lindelof] Talk about eye-acting there.
Evangeline was awesome.

17:47.837 --> 17:49.923
"Hi, my name is Jack Shephard.

17:50.006 --> 17:54.094
- I am an obsessive psychopath."
- [Mitchell] "And I'm lying."

17:54.177 --> 17:56.179
[Lindelof] I love that
he's smiling here.

17:56.263 --> 17:58.181
He's actually enjoying the deception.

17:58.265 --> 18:01.726
[Mitchell] I love what a good liar
he is. It's, I think it's fantastic.

18:01.810 --> 18:04.437
They're both pretty good liars,
really, Jack and Juliet.

18:04.521 --> 18:08.066
[Lindelof] Jack does a lot of lying
in this season. But it's all good lying.

18:08.149 --> 18:10.610
[Mitchell] It's good lying.
No, he's a hot character.

18:10.694 --> 18:13.905
[Lindelof] I tried to explain to my mom
"No, Mom, it's good lying."

18:13.989 --> 18:17.575
- [Mitchell laughs] It's good lying.
- [Lindelof] She never really bought it.

18:17.659 --> 18:19.786
[Mitchell] We got in
a lot of trouble for lying.

18:19.869 --> 18:23.623
[Lindelof] I'm just noticing for the
first time these trophies behind Jack.

18:23.707 --> 18:27.627
And I wonder, what do you...?
They're over sort of to his right.

18:27.711 --> 18:32.382
And I wonder, what do you win a trophy
for if you are a good spinal surgeon?

18:32.465 --> 18:36.136
That's... [laughs]
You know, is it sort of like...

18:36.219 --> 18:38.138
...Best Surgery '02.

18:38.221 --> 18:42.058
"Let me tell you something, Dad.
I not only won the bowling trophy..."

18:42.142 --> 18:44.644
[Mitchell] Best fixing
of a nicked artery.

18:44.728 --> 18:47.063
[Lindelof] "No one fixes
a nicked artery like I do.

18:47.147 --> 18:49.733
I've got the trophy to prove it."

18:49.816 --> 18:53.278
[Mitchell] "Nobody puts Jack
in a corner." And he...

18:53.361 --> 18:54.946
[Mitchell laughing]

18:55.030 --> 18:57.532
Ohh, he's so sad.

18:57.615 --> 19:01.536
[Lindelof] How would you feel if your
daddy was having sex with your ex-wife

19:01.619 --> 19:04.331
who you were obsessively
trying to track down?

19:04.414 --> 19:08.418
[Mitchell] Hey, yeah, now, that,
that was an excellent turn of events.

19:08.501 --> 19:13.048
Look at those blue eyes. Hey,
maybe I'm really his father. [gasps]

19:13.131 --> 19:16.593
[Lindelof] Interesting. They actually
look a lot alike, these two.

19:16.676 --> 19:18.678
[Mitchell] They do look a lot alike.

19:18.762 --> 19:21.890
[Lindelof] John Terry is another guy
who is so awesome in flashbacks

19:21.973 --> 19:25.185
that we regretted killing him
almost instantly, but we were like,

19:25.268 --> 19:28.813
"Oh, we'll just have to see him in
every single effing flashback ever."

19:29.647 --> 19:32.192
[Mitchell] I haven't met him,
but I enjoy watching him.

19:32.275 --> 19:35.028
- [Lindelof] He's awesome.
- [Mitchell] Back to the chains.

19:35.111 --> 19:39.240
That was a creepy set, you know? Damon,
that was a creepy set. I loved it.

19:39.324 --> 19:42.035
And I love that this water
is disgustingly poisonous.

19:42.118 --> 19:44.204
[Lindelof] Zack designed this set.

19:44.287 --> 19:46.998
Um, that's brine,
because Jack is underwater.

19:47.082 --> 19:50.126
And, uh, he doesn't know it yet.
But he's thirsty.

19:51.628 --> 19:56.007
[Mitchell] Is it wrong that this was
a sexy settome? Is it? Am ...

19:56.091 --> 19:58.009
[Lindelof] I wouldn't say wrong

19:58.093 --> 20:00.470
- as much as... you need help.
- [Mitchell laughing]

20:00.553 --> 20:04.182
[Lindelof] And you're
seriously disturbed. But, uh, hey...

20:04.265 --> 20:07.894
[Mitchell] And just stay right where
you are. We're coming to get you.

20:07.977 --> 20:10.230
[Lindelof] That's good. Lights on.

20:10.313 --> 20:13.358
By the way, I like that the Dharma
Initiative took the time to label

20:13.441 --> 20:17.946
their bottled water, just 'cause, "Oh,
we don't want to compete with Evian.

20:18.029 --> 20:21.574
We want you to know that
you're drinking Dharma Initiative water.

20:21.658 --> 20:24.411
Nope. That's not Crystal Geyser.

20:24.494 --> 20:29.040
Mmm. Nothing tastes as good as a nice
bottle of Dharma Initiative water."

20:29.124 --> 20:32.377
- [Mitchell laughing] Oh, no.
- [Lindelof] It's the little things.

20:32.460 --> 20:34.754
[Mitchell] That's very serious stuff,
you know?

20:34.838 --> 20:38.341
[Lindelof] But, honestly, I will say
the toothpicks are awesome here.

20:38.425 --> 20:40.510
And I love the way
that you play this scene.

20:41.511 --> 20:43.721
[Mitchell] I love the toothpicks
as well.

20:43.805 --> 20:46.433
And I love that she doesn't cook...

20:46.516 --> 20:48.726
...or even make the sandwiches.

20:48.810 --> 20:50.437
[Lindelof] She doesn't.

20:50.520 --> 20:54.274
I always imagined that there's some guy
with an iron standing outside the room,

20:54.357 --> 20:57.110
just putting,
sticking it down on a grill,

20:57.193 --> 20:59.612
on a couple pieces of bread
and a piece of cheese.

21:00.196 --> 21:02.198
You can have it.

21:03.700 --> 21:06.286
[Lindelof] It's all in the presentation.

21:06.369 --> 21:08.329
[Mitchell] It's all in the presentation.

21:08.413 --> 21:12.834
What do you do, Jack?
What's your profession?

21:12.917 --> 21:13.960
I'm a repo man.

21:14.043 --> 21:16.921
[Mitchell] It's just so surreal.
The scenes that you wrote,

21:17.005 --> 21:20.175
the reason I liked them so much
when I read them, they're so surreal.

21:21.509 --> 21:24.137
I'm a people person,
so I really love it.

21:24.220 --> 21:26.097
Are you married?

21:26.389 --> 21:30.268
[Mitchell] They start laughing at each
other pretty quickly, which is nice.

21:30.351 --> 21:32.645
[Lindelof] 'Cause she knows everything,

21:32.729 --> 21:35.482
and I love the fact that
you're playing it like she doesn't.

21:35.565 --> 21:38.318
She's not calling "bullcrap" yet.

21:39.235 --> 21:43.656
[Mitchell] I think it's very important
that he tell her the things, actually.

21:43.740 --> 21:45.617
I think it's important to her.

21:45.700 --> 21:49.245
When your plane crashed,
where were you flying from?

21:49.329 --> 21:52.999
[Mitchell] I think he was specifically
trying to show her his muscle there.

21:53.082 --> 21:55.335
[Lindelof] This, uh...
That's a good look.

21:55.418 --> 21:59.839
These, these episodes for us as writers
are almost always about,

21:59.923 --> 22:01.674
what does a character want?

22:01.758 --> 22:04.677
You know, obviously, that tracks
from sort of scene to scene,

22:04.761 --> 22:07.347
and there is sort of
a seasonal arc. But...

22:07.430 --> 22:13.019
I think it's very clear by episode's end
exactly what it is they both want.

22:13.102 --> 22:16.689
Um, and it's so... They have
all these scenes, but, you know,

22:16.773 --> 22:21.819
the idea of basically kind of beginning
to break Jack down, and get him to,

22:21.903 --> 22:24.447
um, start to let go of his past.

22:24.531 --> 22:28.993
And condition him, and getting him in,
into this place of, um,

22:29.077 --> 22:32.163
you know, as far as Juliet is concerned,
getting him into a place

22:32.247 --> 22:35.416
where she can get him to kill Ben,
although she doesn't realize,

22:35.500 --> 22:38.461
she doesn't reveal that agenda
for several episodes.

22:38.545 --> 22:42.173
Um, Ben's agenda is to get Jack
to perform the surgery.

22:42.257 --> 22:46.386
So this episode, Ben and Juliet
want exactly the same thing,

22:46.469 --> 22:48.972
um, although for different reasons.

22:49.055 --> 22:52.392
Mitchell] For different reasons,
yeah, I love that.

23:00.066 --> 23:04.529
- This was hard, right in front of him.
- [Lindelof] That was the best.

23:05.405 --> 23:08.241
[Mitchell] It was, you know,
you guys wrote it, and I was like,

23:08.324 --> 23:12.620
"Oh, that's gonna be hard." But it,
It was kind of fun to do once we did it.

23:13.621 --> 23:17.250
[Lindelof] I like the sound of biting
into a grilled cheese sandwich.

23:18.418 --> 23:22.213
[Mitchell laughs] Yeah.
Who doesn't love grilled cheese?

23:22.297 --> 23:24.632
You can just taste it.
It's delicious.

23:26.009 --> 23:29.262
[Lindelof] It's at around this point
in writing the script, I was like,

23:29.345 --> 23:32.599
"Hey, wait a minute, we're almost
half an hour into the first episode,

23:32.682 --> 23:37.437
and no one has received
the massive beating yet." So it...

23:37.520 --> 23:41.107
It just wouldn't be Lost unless
there was a significant beating.

23:41.190 --> 23:43.943
And Karl just looks
so sweet and innocent.

23:44.027 --> 23:46.946
So this is how... He's out.

23:47.030 --> 23:50.116
And you know a beating
is soon to come.

23:50.199 --> 23:54.495
[Mitchell] That was excellent. Man,
that Jack Bender, he really can direct.

23:54.579 --> 23:55.955
He really can.

23:56.039 --> 23:58.041
[Lindelof] He's not bad,
when he's sober.

23:58.124 --> 24:02.420
[Mitchell laughs] No, he's... nice.

24:02.503 --> 24:05.506
[Lindelof] Man, I was drunk
when I wrote this episode.

24:15.141 --> 24:19.187
This, uh, this cue is very Planet
Of The Apes-y, that Giacchino wrote.

24:19.270 --> 24:22.565
Oh, here you are.
You guys shot this, like, weeks later.

24:24.233 --> 24:26.069
[Mitchell] Yeah, we did.

24:28.154 --> 24:32.075
[Lindelof] You're actually tickling Josh
just out of frame there, aren't you?

24:32.158 --> 24:33.910
That's how he was able to...

24:33.993 --> 24:36.496
- He's also Method.
- [Mitchell] Yeah, of course.

24:36.579 --> 24:38.081
I think they both might have been

24:38.164 --> 24:40.667
a little afraid of me
in this first episode.

24:40.750 --> 24:43.336
I try to do my best
to stay back a little.

24:46.047 --> 24:50.009
I love, by the way, you know,
she's totally into Jack,

24:50.093 --> 24:54.681
but she just doesn't, she's not...
Sawyer's powers do not work on Juliet.

24:54.764 --> 24:57.684
[Mitchell] That's really true, isn't it?
I wonder why that is,

24:57.767 --> 25:00.061
but it's been that way
from the very beginning.

25:01.771 --> 25:04.691
I think maybe that she's...
I don't know.

25:04.774 --> 25:07.443
She's kind of past
the whole Sawyer thing.

25:07.527 --> 25:09.696
Like, he's so...
As I said a million times...

25:09.779 --> 25:12.448
[Lindelof] She is. He's just
not as interesting to her.

25:12.532 --> 25:15.952
[Mitchell] Jack is far more interesting
to her. She sees him for what he is.

25:16.035 --> 25:18.413
She's just not, it's not her thing.

25:21.040 --> 25:22.083
I think that...

25:22.166 --> 25:25.503
- [Lindelof] And here he is again.
- [Mitchell] I know, he's very sad.

25:27.338 --> 25:30.883
[Lindelof] It's amazing that Matthew,
basically, had to sit in that room

25:30.967 --> 25:35.555
for six episodes, pretty much, of work,
and didn't go entirely bonkers.

25:35.638 --> 25:38.725
[Mitchell] I was really hoping
I'd get to be in that cage for a while,

25:38.808 --> 25:40.101
I have to admit.

25:41.477 --> 25:43.604
- [Lindelof] Why?
- [Mitchell] I don't know.

25:43.688 --> 25:47.108
There was something dramatic about it.
I guess 'cause I'm a theatre actor.

25:47.191 --> 25:50.695
You guys set it up
like a beautiful play. It was fun.

25:50.778 --> 25:52.488
It was really fun to do.

25:54.240 --> 25:56.743
[Lindelof] This is back
to the sexy thing isn't it?

25:56.826 --> 25:59.370
- [Mitchell] Well...
- [Lindelof] You and that cage.

25:59.454 --> 26:02.999
[Mitchell] Yeah, I think so. I think
I might have a thing for the cage.

26:04.167 --> 26:07.754
[Lindelof] I love that moment, by the
way, when she says, "I'm a repo woman."

26:07.837 --> 26:09.088
[Mitchell] And he laughs.

26:09.172 --> 26:11.924
[Lindelof] The subtext there is,
you sneaky little devil.

26:12.008 --> 26:14.969
He holds up his finger,
and he's kind of like, you know, touché

26:15.052 --> 26:17.180
[Mitchell] Yeah, he really is. [laughs]

26:20.349 --> 26:23.770
[Lindelof] Now she's really
starting to wear him down. It's...

26:23.853 --> 26:27.815
It's such an effective,
um, "I really believe you" here.

26:27.899 --> 26:31.277
[Mitchell] It's the only tactic that
would work for him, though, because

26:31.360 --> 26:34.280
if she came at him hard,
he'd come right back.

26:34.363 --> 26:37.825
So it's really the only thing that
would work, is to go underneath.

26:40.870 --> 26:42.288
You can tell that he's...

26:42.371 --> 26:45.291
- [Lindelof] Is it gonna work?
- [Mitchell] With women, he's...

26:45.374 --> 26:47.335
Yeah, I think it's working.

26:47.418 --> 26:49.545
Juliet thinks it's working.

26:49.629 --> 26:53.132
- Look at that, he looks beaten.
- [Lindelof] That fruit sure looks good.

26:53.216 --> 26:56.427
[Mitchell] It looks really good,
plenty of water in there.

26:56.511 --> 27:00.807
[Lindelof] "Here, Jack.
Come on. Here, Jack."

27:00.890 --> 27:03.768
But he is like,
"No, I'm gonna go sit in the corner."

27:03.851 --> 27:07.647
[Mitchell] No, that's not gonna happen.
Something crazy is gonna happen.

27:08.606 --> 27:10.942
And she's just
slightly disappointed.

27:11.025 --> 27:13.236
[Mitchell sighs]

27:13.319 --> 27:17.740
[Lindelof] Little does she know, Jack is
hatching a secret plan. He's lied again.

27:17.824 --> 27:19.784
[Mitchell] You think? Oh, come on.

27:19.867 --> 27:22.119
[Lindelof] I wouldn't trust him.

27:22.203 --> 27:23.871
[Mitchell] Really?

27:27.583 --> 27:30.127
[Lindelof] I'd let him
operate on me, though.

27:30.211 --> 27:34.507
[Mitchell] Well, I would if he weren't
incapacitated or obsessed, absolutely.

27:34.590 --> 27:37.426
- [Lindelof] Not Jack, Matthew Fox.
- [Mitchell laughing]

27:37.510 --> 27:41.514
Listen, from what I know about
Matthew Fox, he could probably do it.

27:41.597 --> 27:45.226
[Lindelof] Yeah. Just, just make sure
you got your eye on your kidney sac.

27:45.309 --> 27:46.769
[Mitchell laughs]

27:46.853 --> 27:50.940
[Lindelof] Be careful, 'cause he will,
he will cut you... He will cut you good.

27:51.023 --> 27:53.025
[Mitchell] He will slice it up.

27:53.109 --> 27:57.947
Oh, no, man. Oh.
Oh, this is all really hard to watch.

27:59.240 --> 28:02.076
[Lindelof] Why? He's going
to have an affair with Sarah.

28:02.159 --> 28:06.163
[Mitchell] I know, but you hate watching
him go down that road, it's so real.

28:06.247 --> 28:10.126
You so get it.
And it's so weak and so sad.

28:10.209 --> 28:13.004
But it does make him so human,
which is nice.

28:13.963 --> 28:17.383
[Lindelof] Yeah, I love, you know,
what's really cool about this episode

28:17.466 --> 28:19.886
is you realize that,
if not for Jack's obsession,

28:19.969 --> 28:23.097
his father might have
gotten things together.

28:23.180 --> 28:25.474
- And, uh...
- [Mitchell] It's really true.

28:25.558 --> 28:27.560
[Lindelof] It's the cycle of despair.

28:27.643 --> 28:28.728
[Mitchell] Yeah.

28:28.811 --> 28:32.106
[Lindelof] You don't even see where
he is yet. And it's like, obviously,

28:32.189 --> 28:33.858
he's not here with your...

28:33.941 --> 28:36.903
- ...wife, dude.
- [Mitchell] No.

28:36.986 --> 28:40.907
[Lindelof] "You're having sex with all
of these people, Dad? All of them?!

28:40.990 --> 28:43.910
What kind of, what kind of
sick meeting is this?"

28:43.993 --> 28:47.163
[Mitchell] Oh. And he can't back off
"cause he's already so mad.

28:47.246 --> 28:49.248
He's already worked up in it.

28:49.332 --> 28:52.460
[Lindelof] In poker,
we call this pot-committed.

28:52.543 --> 28:56.339
[Mitchell] Pot... Yes,
oh, that's excellent. Yeah.

28:56.422 --> 29:00.134
[Lindelof] And it basically means you've
put so much money in on the bluff

29:00.217 --> 29:05.097
that you cannot fold your cards.
And that's where Jack is right now.

29:05.181 --> 29:07.141
It's kind of like, "OK, I was wrong,

29:07.224 --> 29:09.894
but now I'm gonna yell at you
about something else."

29:10.853 --> 29:13.856
My marriage? What'd you tell them
about my marriage, Dad?

29:13.940 --> 29:16.692
[Mitchell] Yeah, I know that's...
Ohh... Oh, he is good.

29:16.776 --> 29:19.320
You know how he manages his marriage?

29:19.403 --> 29:21.948
A bottle of Scotch every night
before dinner.

29:22.031 --> 29:24.951
Your father has been sober
50 days now.

29:25.534 --> 29:27.620
[Mitchell] But if you're
gonna break down,

29:27.703 --> 29:30.456
an AA meeting is probably
a good place to do it.

29:30.539 --> 29:33.376
[Lindelof] ] They're kind of used to it.
But Jack's not even,

29:33.459 --> 29:38.047
you know, Jack doesn't even, even
get to say he's drunk here. He's, he...

29:38.130 --> 29:40.132
...he detonates sober.

29:40.216 --> 29:44.095
[Mitchell] If he had just started with
a "Hello, my name is Jack, I'm a..."

29:44.178 --> 29:46.263
all this would be OK.

29:46.347 --> 29:48.474
[Lindelof] And they'd all say,
"Hello, Jack."

29:48.557 --> 29:51.727
I don't think the scene
would have been as interesting.

29:51.811 --> 29:53.813
[Mitchell] Damon,
you know, you're right,

29:53.896 --> 29:56.273
but I'm just trying
to give you some colors here.

29:57.024 --> 29:59.402
Oh, and now I'm gonna
give him some food.

29:59.485 --> 30:02.196
[inhales] Ooh, it's a little
nerve-racking now.

30:02.279 --> 30:05.950
[Lindelof] Less interesting version of
this scene. Jack just lets her come in,

30:06.033 --> 30:09.829
- puts the fruit down...
- [Mitchell] And says hi. Oh, goodnight.

30:09.912 --> 30:12.164
[Lindelof] No, but he always
has to run at people.

30:20.047 --> 30:23.217
[Mitchell] You know, we ended up having
to use the real plate because

30:23.300 --> 30:26.929
the rubber one they had kept bending
every time he put it to my throat.

30:27.013 --> 30:30.933
- [Lindelof] Oh, my God.
- [Mitchell] This was a trust exercise.

30:31.017 --> 30:32.768
It was actually pretty funny.

30:32.852 --> 30:35.855
[Lindelof] I love that Jack's
doing a little MacGyver here.

30:35.938 --> 30:38.691
Who would have thought that
you could use a plate as a weapon?

30:38.774 --> 30:40.651
[Mitchell laughs] I know.

30:40.735 --> 30:44.822
[Lindelof] "I swear to God, I will
make you eat off this broken plate."

30:44.905 --> 30:47.116
[Mitchell laughs]

30:49.618 --> 30:52.121
[Mitchell] Here's where
he betrays her, which I love,

30:52.204 --> 30:53.998
and she appreciates this.

30:55.541 --> 30:58.210
Oh! Oh! Oh!

30:58.294 --> 31:01.130
Man, if she didn't hate him before...

31:01.213 --> 31:04.633
She's gonna kick his ass.
Excuse my language.

31:04.717 --> 31:07.011
- But come on.
- [Lindelof] I think you can say ass.

31:07.094 --> 31:08.054
You're allowed.

31:08.137 --> 31:10.389
- [Mitchell] Can you?
- [Lindelof] You said it.

31:10.473 --> 31:13.517
[Mitchell whispers] OK. Thanks.
I did? I know.

31:13.601 --> 31:16.812
[Lindelof] I love that Jack lets her go,
and he is like, you know what?

31:16.896 --> 31:18.522
Now, let me ask you something.

31:18.606 --> 31:22.359
When is the last time you turned a
handle like that and this didn't happen?

31:22.443 --> 31:26.906
Huh? 'Cause chances are if you're
if you're turning a handle like that...

31:26.989 --> 31:28.407
...you're gonna get wet.

31:28.491 --> 31:31.494
[Mitchell] Something,
something bad is gonna happen.

31:31.577 --> 31:35.164
Yeah. Something's behind that door
that ain't supposed to get out.

31:35.247 --> 31:39.627
[Mitchell] Thought we should get to
know each other. And she saves him.

31:39.710 --> 31:41.087
She saves him.

31:41.170 --> 31:43.422
[Lindelof] Was this
fun to shoot or petrifying?

31:43.506 --> 31:46.342
[Mitchell] This was so...
No, there was nothing petrifying.

31:46.425 --> 31:49.845
But any time you get to do
your own stunts, it's thrilling.

31:49.929 --> 31:54.391
I mean, I feel bad for the stunt person.
But, uh, she was very gracious about it.

31:54.475 --> 31:56.268
But it's so interesting because

31:56.352 --> 31:59.230
you're in it with the other
actor and there's no faking.

31:59.313 --> 32:02.441
You're doing exactly what you're
supposed to do. It's so much fun.

32:03.859 --> 32:07.696
[Lindelof] Hey, how long has it been
since somebody got beat up on this show?

32:07.780 --> 32:09.782
[Mitchell laughs]

32:09.865 --> 32:12.618
[Lindelof] I think it's been
almost six minutes.

32:12.701 --> 32:14.328
[Mitchell shouts] Nice!

32:14.411 --> 32:17.373
You know, I was supposed
to originally punch him in the stomach.

32:17.456 --> 32:19.583
That wasn't...
You know who helped me do that,

32:19.667 --> 32:22.711
Matthew and I came up with that
together, because I was supposed to

32:22.795 --> 32:26.006
punch him in the stomach and
he fell over. And it just wasn't as...

32:26.090 --> 32:29.635
Now, this wasn't in the script.
That was just something that we did

32:29.718 --> 32:30.427
and we thought was getting cut.
But he was down, not breathing,

32:30.427 --> 32:33.472
and we thought was getting cut.
But he was down, not breathing,

32:33.556 --> 32:36.600
you know what I mean? In the water.
I thought, we should pick him up.

32:36.684 --> 32:38.602
- I like it now.
- [Lindelof] I love that,

32:38.686 --> 32:40.271
and it's like, "poor Jack."

32:40.354 --> 32:43.190
[Mitchell] Yeah. 'Cause what
I was told was we'd never use it.

32:43.274 --> 32:46.110
And I was so... It was so
amazing that it was in there.

32:46.193 --> 32:49.238
[Lindelof] When you make awesome
choices, we put them in the show

32:49.321 --> 32:50.739
and then take credit for them.

32:50.823 --> 32:54.285
[Mitchell laughs] Sorry.
I shouldn't have said that.

32:54.368 --> 32:56.662
[Lindelof] No, I think it was
an awesome idea.

32:56.745 --> 32:59.832
Maybe you should just
start writing this show, Elizabeth.

33:00.833 --> 33:04.253
[laugh] Damon, stop.
Thank God I don't.

33:04.336 --> 33:07.339
[Lindelof] I think that was...
You guys make choices all the time

33:07.423 --> 33:09.884
that we exploit and, uh, you know...

33:09.967 --> 33:12.845
But you guys are playing
these characters. So...

33:14.013 --> 33:16.807
[Mitchell] Well, you make it,
it's fun. It's more fun.

33:16.891 --> 33:18.851
It's more fun than I've ever had.

33:18.934 --> 33:21.270
[Lindelof] Really?
I hope that's not true.

33:21.353 --> 33:25.399
[Mitchell] Yeah. It's more fun than I've
ever had in a show. Yeah, absolutely.

33:25.482 --> 33:27.443
This is the most fun. It's a fun show.

33:27.526 --> 33:30.112
It's fun words, and it's a ridiculously
good character.

33:30.196 --> 33:33.365
[Lindelof] Dharma Initiative needs
to label their fish biscuits,

33:33.449 --> 33:35.367
'cause God forbid,
the polar bear is like,

33:35.451 --> 33:38.871
"Hey, where can I get another
fish biscuit like this? Oh."

33:38.954 --> 33:42.374
I'm starting to think that Dharma
Initiative were egotistical maniacs,

33:42.458 --> 33:45.878
- they stick their names on everything.
- [Mitchell] I think you're right.

33:45.961 --> 33:48.881
[Lindelof] Sawyer should be like,
"This ain't Dharma water!"

33:48.964 --> 33:52.509
- [mock spitting] And spit it out.
- [Mitchell laughs]

33:52.593 --> 33:55.638
- [Mitchell] Oh, look.
- [Lindelof] This is a great moment.

33:55.721 --> 34:00.351
[Mitchell] Oh, it is beautiful. They do
the most beautiful work together.

34:00.434 --> 34:04.855
Ohh... And he doesn't know
what happened and she's in a dress.

34:05.981 --> 34:08.192
Oh, his heart's breaking.

34:08.776 --> 34:12.196
Stick your hands out through the bars,
I'll take off your cuffs.

34:12.279 --> 34:15.324
Scratched you up pretty bad,
didn't they?

34:15.407 --> 34:18.160
I'll bring you some antiseptic later.

34:18.244 --> 34:20.037
[Lindelof] Ahh, that's nice of you.

34:20.120 --> 34:22.498
<i>While you're at it,
I could use a blow-dry.</i>

34:22.581 --> 34:25.417
[Lindelof] That's a J. J. Abrams line
all the way.

34:26.168 --> 34:28.545
[Mitchell laughs] I swear,
that's freaking funny.

34:28.629 --> 34:31.257
[Lindelof] If anybody appreciates
a blow-dry, it's J.J.

34:31.340 --> 34:33.926
[Mitchell] He should be on the cover
of a romance novel.

34:34.009 --> 34:35.761
It's... Oh, J.J.

34:35.844 --> 34:39.348
He's so nice.
I had no idea, but he's so nice.

34:40.015 --> 34:42.309
- [Lindelof] He sure is.
- [Mitchell] Oh, guys.

34:46.188 --> 34:48.691
Oh, this is sad.

34:49.191 --> 34:52.319
- You?
- Just swell.

34:53.279 --> 34:56.657
I requested that cage, but whatever.

34:56.740 --> 34:59.159
[Lindelof] Nothing like a good joke
to break the ice.

34:59.243 --> 35:02.371
[Mitchell laughing]

35:04.748 --> 35:07.960
Nice dress.

35:08.043 --> 35:10.671
They made me wear it.

35:12.464 --> 35:15.426
- [Lindelof] He doesn't like that.
- [Mitchell] Oh, my God.

35:15.509 --> 35:18.804
No. Ohh.

35:19.263 --> 35:20.764
You hungry?

35:23.475 --> 35:26.103
[Lindelof] This is a perfect example
of awesome acting,

35:26.186 --> 35:28.105
because we write the dialogue here,

35:28.188 --> 35:30.816
but all the great stuff
is happening around the lines,

35:30.899 --> 35:33.986
you know, it's all these looks that
they're throwing at each other.

35:34.069 --> 35:36.655
[Mitchell] Yeah, they did.
They got an amazing thing.

35:36.739 --> 35:39.033
They are so much fun to watch.

35:40.576 --> 35:43.746
[Lindelof] I like that she covers
her mouth there. It's kind of like,

35:43.829 --> 35:48.083
it's this sort of demure moment in the
midst of complete and utter insanity.

35:48.917 --> 35:51.337
[Mitchell] It really is.
It's just lovely.

35:51.420 --> 35:54.298
And you get back to these two.
Oh, dear.

35:58.010 --> 35:59.595
[groaning]

36:01.305 --> 36:03.640
[Mitchell snickers]

36:04.767 --> 36:07.603
[Mitchell] Now I look like
the high school principal.

36:08.437 --> 36:12.316
[Lindelof] So can you elaborate just
a little more on when you met Matthew?

36:12.399 --> 36:15.277
Obviously, he had kind of read
the script. You came down there.

36:15.361 --> 36:18.238
You alluded to the fact
that you sort of iced him.

36:18.322 --> 36:21.533
Is that really how it went down?
When did you, when did you...?

36:21.617 --> 36:25.662
[Mitchell] No, I didn't necessarily ice
him. I said a few words to him

36:25.746 --> 36:28.957
that were kind words. And he said a
few words to me that were kind words,

36:29.041 --> 36:32.169
and then for the remainder
of the episode,

36:32.252 --> 36:35.047
we didn't speak to each other
except to talk about the scenes.

36:35.130 --> 36:40.094
And it was incredibly helpful because,
uh, all of it was just Jack and Juliet.

36:40.177 --> 36:43.180
I have no, I had no idea who
Matthew was. He had no idea who I was.

36:43.263 --> 36:48.060
So it was just us. And I have to say, as
odd as that sounds, it was incredibly,

36:48.143 --> 36:50.854
uh, it made it,
made things a lot easier.

36:50.938 --> 36:53.732
[Lindelof] And what was your
experience like with Josh?

36:53.816 --> 36:57.403
- Was it, uh, was it wildly different?
- [Mitchell] Oh, Josh. [laughs]

36:57.486 --> 37:01.407
I think he probably heard from Matthew
that I was kind of dry,

37:01.490 --> 37:04.368
so Josh might have been
a little afraid. But he was,

37:04.451 --> 37:08.455
he was really quite lovely, and, and
I was still very much in the stages of,

37:08.539 --> 37:11.834
you know, we weren't sure where
Juliet was coming from. So, again,

37:11.917 --> 37:14.086
a few kind words
and a few kind words and then,

37:14.169 --> 37:16.922
I kind of backed off a little
and let everyone do their thing.

37:18.173 --> 37:20.843
But, uh, it's a little different now.
[laughs]

37:20.926 --> 37:24.596
[Lindelof] Every season we obviously
introduce new characters onto the show.

37:24.680 --> 37:26.932
And there's this infrastructure
down in Hawaii.

37:27.015 --> 37:29.351
Obviously, these guys
have been down there since,

37:29.435 --> 37:32.646
you know, since we shot the pilot.
So they're their own kind of,

37:32.729 --> 37:35.274
you know, they're the,
you know, they're the seniors,

37:35.357 --> 37:37.609
and you're coming in kind of
as a freshman.

37:37.693 --> 37:40.529
It's almost like in this case,
because they're the Others,

37:40.612 --> 37:43.699
and they've actually been on the island
longer than the castaways,

37:43.782 --> 37:46.618
it's not like the tail section.
So it's almost like what's...

37:46.702 --> 37:49.455
What I love about the dynamic
is kind of Juliet is the senior

37:49.538 --> 37:53.417
and Jack is the freshman,
even though we've never seen her before.

37:53.500 --> 37:56.128
[Mitchell] You know your crew
and you know how they are.

37:56.211 --> 37:58.964
And they are the most giving
group of people.

37:59.047 --> 38:03.635
So they were very lovely to let me
come in and kind of be this person.

38:03.719 --> 38:07.639
They definitely gave, gave the power
to me, which was so, so nice of them.

38:07.723 --> 38:10.476
But it, it made it work.
But it's a nice dynamic.

38:10.559 --> 38:13.979
I think it... It's a great way
to come into a show,

38:14.062 --> 38:18.233
'cause you're not trying to be one
of them. You're something else entirely.

38:19.401 --> 38:21.028
Ohh.

38:21.111 --> 38:25.199
I thought he was so,
so delicious in this, in this episode.

38:25.908 --> 38:27.326
He just wowed me.

38:27.409 --> 38:30.787
[Lindelof] Would you say he is as
delicious as a grilled cheese sandwich?

38:30.871 --> 38:34.458
[Mitchell] Oh, maybe even more,
Damon, maybe even more.

38:34.541 --> 38:36.084
[Lindelof] Wow.

38:37.544 --> 38:40.839
What do you think would happen
if you put a toothpick in Matthew?

38:40.923 --> 38:44.009
[Mitchell laughs] Oh,
let's not go there.

38:44.092 --> 38:46.637
[Mitchell laughing]

38:47.429 --> 38:49.348
Someone posted your bail.

38:50.015 --> 38:52.184
[Lindelof] We actually
moved the positioning

38:52.267 --> 38:55.103
of this flashback in the show,
as we so often do in editing,

38:55.187 --> 38:59.358
and, you know, I love that,
I love that it's like, it's just,

38:59.441 --> 39:02.861
in that she basically asked that
question, now you show all this stuff

39:02.945 --> 39:06.865
"cause you're kind of wondering,
you know, how this all ended up.

39:06.949 --> 39:09.868
- And here is where, you know...
- [Mitchell] And now he finds out

39:09.952 --> 39:12.788
- what he did to his father.
- [Lindelof] It's excruciating.

39:13.413 --> 39:16.166
[Mitchell] Oh, God.
It's so heartbreaking, this.

39:16.250 --> 39:20.045
I'm so surprised that Matthew didn't
get nominated for something here.

39:20.128 --> 39:22.422
I really thought this episode
was exemplary.

39:22.506 --> 39:25.717
[Lindelof] Um, I don't think he,
uh, I don't think this episode was,

39:25.801 --> 39:28.887
uh, you know, this qualifies
for this year coming up.

39:28.971 --> 39:33.016
So, you know, maybe he did get nominated
and we just don't realize it yet,

39:33.100 --> 39:35.978
- 'cause we're doing this...
- [Mitchell] Just don't know yet.

39:36.061 --> 39:38.855
- I thought he was so good.
- [Lindelof] He does awesome work.

39:38.939 --> 39:41.483
- Is that him?
- What difference does it make?

39:41.567 --> 39:44.570
[Lindelof] He's already got
all those trophies. So, you know...

39:45.112 --> 39:48.532
- What do you need another one for?
- [Mitchell] Slam dancing.

39:48.615 --> 39:52.369
It doesn't matter who he is.
It just matters who you're not.

39:52.452 --> 39:56.415
[Lindelof] I love that. I love that she,
I love that she delivers that line

39:56.498 --> 39:59.793
in such anguish.
It's, like, not mean at all.

39:59.876 --> 40:02.337
[Mitchell] She just, she's so good.

40:07.926 --> 40:11.263
...he was so drunk
I could hardly understand him.

40:11.346 --> 40:13.765
[Lindelof] And you can
see his reaction there.

40:13.849 --> 40:18.103
It's like she just pulled
a hair out of his... I don't know,

40:18.186 --> 40:20.606
some place that it hurts a lot.

40:21.690 --> 40:23.442
[Mitchell] Hmm, something,

40:23.525 --> 40:25.902
Now you have something to fix.

40:27.863 --> 40:30.532
[Mitchell] Some place
way under the skin.

40:32.200 --> 40:35.537
[Lindelof] And I love that we don't
even see this guy. He doesn't matter.

40:37.122 --> 40:40.751
He's just a... That's, that's what
the story was supposed to be about,

40:40.834 --> 40:45.005
but, and here we go.
This breaks my heart every time.

40:45.631 --> 40:46.757
[Mitchell] Me too.

40:46.840 --> 40:49.343
[Lindelof] 'Cause she knows
what he's gonna ask.

40:50.719 --> 40:53.055
[Mitchell] Yeah, she does.

40:56.058 --> 40:58.226
Is she happy?

41:00.354 --> 41:05.150
Yes, Jack, she's very happy.

41:05.233 --> 41:09.029
[Lindelof] And I'm not sure
Juliet actually knows that for a fact.

41:11.490 --> 41:15.118
I think it's just like I, and your
performance, I think it's kind of like,

41:15.202 --> 41:18.622
I know this is what you need to hear,
buddy, and I'm gonna give it to you,

41:18.705 --> 41:21.291
not because I'm trying to coerce you,

41:21.375 --> 41:24.503
but it's because you need
something good.

41:24.586 --> 41:29.091
[Mitchell] It's a human thing. Yeah.
Yeah, it's a human thing at this point.

41:29.174 --> 41:32.260
That's where she starts
to like him, I think.

41:34.262 --> 41:37.391
[Lindelof] I think that plays
when she steps out into the hallway,

41:37.474 --> 41:40.977
'cause there's this tremendous
sense of guilt hanging over her

41:41.061 --> 41:44.439
- already when she talks to Ben.
- [Mitchell] Oh, it's awful.

41:44.523 --> 41:47.901
[Lindelof] It's kind of like, "All
right, I did it. I'm not happy about it.

41:47.984 --> 41:52.656
- You bastard. But it's done."”
- [Mitchell] Yeah.

41:52.739 --> 41:55.534
- But it's done.
- [Lindelof] Great shot. There.

41:55.617 --> 41:56.910
[Mitchell] Jeez.

41:56.993 --> 42:01.456
Well, he's such a big guy,
and to see him like that is so hard.

42:03.333 --> 42:06.878
[Lindelof] He'll get those Others,
though. He'll get them good.

42:06.962 --> 42:10.298
[Mitchell] I think he might.
I have a feeling. [laughs]

42:10.382 --> 42:13.927
[Lindelof] It is cool to watch this
episode and realize that Jack and Juliet

42:14.010 --> 42:16.888
kind of gang-up and join forces
to take all these bastards out

42:16.972 --> 42:20.142
by the end of the season.
And this is the beginning.

42:20.225 --> 42:23.562
[Mitchell] Yeah. Yeah.
No, I really like that.

42:23.645 --> 42:27.023
I also really like that he,
he starts to trust her.

42:28.024 --> 42:29.025
[Mitchell groans]

42:29.109 --> 42:32.696
[Lindelof] By the way, when in doubt,
go off on Michael Emerson's eyes.

42:32.779 --> 42:35.741
You can't go wrong there.
- [Mitchell] Go off... are you kidding?

42:35.824 --> 42:36.116
- Michael Emerson, uh, is amazing.
- [Lindelof] Schroer. OK so...

42:36.116 --> 42:39.494
- Michael Emerson, uh, is amazing.
- [Lindelof] Schroer. OK so...

42:39.578 --> 42:43.248
- Goodbye, everybody. Thank you...
- [Mitchell] Goodbye.

42:43.331 --> 42:47.294
[Lindelof] ...for listening to our
completely non-informative dithering.

42:47.377 --> 42:52.257
- Um, at least speaking personally.
- [Mitchell] Our Mystery Science 30007?

42:52.340 --> 42:55.218
- [Lindelof] Exactly.
- [Mitchell] I can dither with the best.

42:55.302 --> 42:57.763
[Lindelof] I don't even know
what dither means.

42:57.846 --> 43:01.057
